{"v":2,"s":"p","w":8,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Density","b":"<p><b>Density</b> (gustina) is mass per unit volume:</p><div class=\"fx\">ρ = m / V   [kg/m³]   1 g/cm³ = 1000 kg/m³</div><table class=\"mini\"><tr><td>water</td><td>1000 kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>quartz</td><td>2650</td></tr><tr><td>granite</td><td>≈ 2700</td></tr><tr><td>iron</td><td>7870</td></tr><tr><td>gold</td><td>19 300</td></tr></table><div class=\"callout geo\">Geology link: density helps identify minerals — a heavy, shiny grain in sand is a hint of gold or pyrite.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"In water (1000 kg/m³): wood (600) floats high, ice (920) floats mostly under water, granite (2700) sinks.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"40\" width=\"260\" height=\"100\" rx=\"4\" class=\"wt\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"40\" class=\"km\" /><rect x=\"60\" y=\"30\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" class=\"ge\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"10\">wood</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"32\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" class=\"ic\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"10\">ice</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"116\" width=\"46\" height=\"24\" rx=\"2\" class=\"mu\"/><text x=\"243\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"10\">granite</text></svg><figcaption>In water (1000 kg/m³): wood (600) floats high, ice (920) floats mostly under water, granite (2700) sinks.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Pressure","b":"<p><b>Pressure</b> (pritisak) is force per unit area:</p><div class=\"fx\">p = F / S   [Pa = N/m²]</div><p>A small area means huge pressure — that’s how knives and nails work. Atmospheric pressure is about 101 325 Pa ≈ 100 kPa.</p><div class=\"callout\">A stiletto heel versus an elephant’s foot: the heel can damage a floor the elephant wouldn’t.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The same brick, the same weight: standing on its small face it presses harder, because p = F / S.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"60\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"56\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"10\">large area → small p</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"20\" width=\"36\" height=\"80\" rx=\"3\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"238\" y1=\"4\" x2=\"238\" y2=\"16\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"238\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"10\">small area → large p</text><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"100\" class=\"km\" /></svg><figcaption>The same brick, the same weight: standing on its small face it presses harder, because p = F / S.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A 1000 kg block stands on a 2 m × 0.5 m base (g = 10). Pressure?","s":["F = mg = 10 000 N.","S = 2 · 0.5 = 1 m².","p = 10 000 / 1."],"a":"10 000 Pa"},{"t":"num","q":"A sample of 600 g has a volume of 200 cm³. Density in g/cm³?","a":3,"u":"g/cm³","e":"600/200."},{"t":"num","q":"Mass of 0.5 m³ of water?","a":500,"u":"kg","e":"1000 · 0.5."},{"t":"num","q":"800 N on 0.02 m². Pressure?","a":40000,"u":"Pa","e":"800/0.02."},{"t":"mc","q":"Which sinks in water?","o":["wood (600 kg/m³)","ice (920 kg/m³)","granite (2700 kg/m³)","cork (240 kg/m³)"],"a":2,"e":"Denser than water (1000 kg/m³) sinks."},{"t":"num","q":"2.65 g/cm³ in kg/m³?","a":2650,"u":"kg/m³","e":"×1000."}]}